 QM,  the  Quasimodo  level,  a  structural  reversal.  In  a  bullish  QM,  price  makes  a  lower  low,  then  breaks  above  the  last  high.  That's  the  market  structure  shift.  The  QM  level  is  the  shoulder,  the  last  swing  low  before  that  lower  low.  To  draw  it,  mark  that  shoulder  and  extend  the  line  to  the  right.  Example  on  gold.  Price  shifts  structure,  pulls  back  to  retest  the  QM,  reverses  with  momentum,  and  continues  higher.  The  bearish  QM  is  the  mirror  image.  Shift,  retest,  reversal,  continuation.  Six  key  levels.  Save  this 
